WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:05.360
Global Referendum Strategy Humanity downloaded TikTok over four billion times to watch strangers twerk.

2
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:11.300
Getting two hundred and eighty million people to click 'yes' on not dying should be easier.

3
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:17.300
Here's how, with math. Politicians can ignore protests. They can ignore polls.

4
00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:24.180
They can ignore reality for surprisingly long periods (see: climate change, nineteen seventy to present).

5
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:32.600
They cannot ignore two hundred and eighty million cryptographically verified humans saying "do this thing or we vote you

6
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.960
out.". Not because they care about those humans. Because they can count.

7
00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:45.860
What You're Actually Building. The Goal. A website where people say "please stop letting me die of stupid things" in a way

8
00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:51.050
that lawyers find convincing. On Wishonia, we would not need a website for this.

9
00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:57.480
We would say "please stop letting me die of stupid things" and then someone would stop letting us die of stupid things.

10
00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:05.040
On your planet, this requires cryptographic verification, because your species lies about everything, including whether

11
00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.800
it wants to be alive. You need mathematical proof that people prefer living.

12
00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:18.820
Think about that sentence for a moment. You have built a civilization where "I don't want to die" requires a receipt.

13
00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:27.440
Requirements: the votes have to be real (auditable), the votes have to be secret (privacy-preserving), the system has to

14
00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:34.080
work for everyone including people without bank accounts or government I.D.s (which is most of Earth, a fact that surprises

15
00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:41.000
the people with bank accounts), the code has to be open-source so anyone can audit it, and the whole thing has to grow fast

16
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.080
enough to matter before your species gets distracted by a new television show.

17
00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:53.000
Target: three point five percent global participation (two hundred and eighty million plus verified votes).

18
00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:58.660
That number isn't arbitrary. It's the number at which politicians start losing sleep.

19
00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:05.980
More on that later. The Voting System. The system uses end-to-end verifiable cryptography.

20
00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:10.740
Each voter gets a receipt that proves they voted, without proving how they voted.

21
00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:17.460
This is called a "zero-knowledge proof," which sounds like something a philosophy student made up during an exam they didn't

22
00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:23.440
study for, but it's real mathematics, and it works, and politicians cannot argue with it.

23
00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:31.820
Several have tried. The math won every time. Math is undefeated against politicians, which is the only undefeated record

24
00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:36.040
in your species' history. Every ballot published anonymized.

25
00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:40.460
Biometric data never leaves your device. All code open-source.

26
00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:47.080
The system is designed so that even the people running it can't see how you voted, which makes it more private than your

27
00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:53.660
actual elections, where the voting booth has a curtain that stops two feet off the ground and the poll worker is definitely

28
00:02:53.660 --> 00:03:00.740
looking at your shoes. On Stopping People from Cheating. Your species has been cheating at democracy since you invented

29
00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:04.930
it. The Athenians had ballot-stuffing. The Romans had vote-buying.

30
00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:11.200
Americans have gerrymandering, which is the practice of drawing voting districts in shapes that look like someone dropped

31
00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.620
a plate of spaghetti on a map and then legally required it.

32
00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:19.920
Three verification layers. Because one has never been enough for you.

33
00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:27.220
Layer one is the bouncer at the door. Email and phone verification, device fingerprinting, I.P.

34
00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:35.100
geolocation. Stops about ninety percent of fraud, which is the lazy fraud, which is most fraud, because cheating, like everything

35
00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:42.380
else your species does, follows a power law where most of the cheating is done by amateurs who give up if you ask them to

36
00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:46.900
verify their phone number. This is the "are you a human" layer.

37
00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:53.940
The bar is low. The fact that it catches ninety percent of attempts tells you something about the sophistication of your

38
00:03:53.940 --> 00:04:00.440
average cheater. Layer two is the V.I.P. section. Government e-I.D.

39
00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:11.260
integration (Estonia, India's Aadhaar, E.U. Electronic Identification, Authentication and Trust Services, or e.I.D.A.S.,

40
00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:19.880
U.S. via I.D. dot me), biometric liveness detection (blink at the camera to prove you're not a photograph, which is a sentence

41
00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:28.400
that would confuse every human who lived before twenty ten), and proof-of-uniqueness partners like Worldcoin, BrightID,

42
00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:37.600
and Gitcoin Passport. Higher trust, higher rewards. This is the "are you a specific human who hasn't already voted as a

43
00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:45.660
different specific human" layer. Layer three is for the billions of humans who don't exist in any database because their

44
00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:48.940
governments can't be bothered to write down that they're alive.

45
00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:56.920
Community attestation: your neighbors confirm you're real. This works because lying to a computer is easy but lying to a

46
00:04:56.920 --> 00:05:03.540
room full of people who watched you eat breakfast is hard. Even Layer one gets you counted.

47
00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:07.140
You don't need a passport to say "I would prefer not to die."

48
00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:14.020
A.I. fraud detection: over ninety-nine percent detection, under one percent false positives.

49
00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:18.880
Biometric data stays on your device, encrypted with keys you control.

50
00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:27.620
Compliant with the General Data Protection Regulation, or G.D.P.R., the California Consumer Privacy Act and California Privacy

51
00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:38.940
Rights Act, or C.C.P.A. and C.P.R.A., the Biometric Information Privacy Act, or B.I.P.A., and the Children's Online Privacy

52
00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:47.640
Protection Act, or C.O.P.P.A. Four different laws from four different places that all say "don't be creepy with people's

53
00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:55.990
